React- react is a open source js library used to build single page 
application

why react
virtual dom- its a copy of real dom---comparision using diffing 
            -this entire process is called reconcialation

single page applicaton - only one index.html

component based architecture- reusabe components -which reduces the code

components- 
it is a reusable piece of code that renders part of UI

types of components
class components-life cycle methods

functional components- hooks (built in functions)



react renders page only whenever the state changes

state 
it is a like a variable which stores the data and which handle dynamic data of
the component

useState()
it is a hook(built in function) that is used to manage the state

import {useState} from 'react'

let [state,setState]=useState(initialvalue)

let [count,setCount]=useState(0)

notes
count---it is a state which holds the data
setCount---it is a function which controls the count value


useEffect()
it is a hook that is used to manage side effects of a react application
such as api calling, settimeout ,setinterval and localstorage

three types of useEffect
1) useEffect without any depenedency- it will run every time whenever the state changes


import {useEffect} from 'react'

async function getapidata(){
    //api logic
}
useEffect(()=>{
    getapidata()
})


2) useEffect with empty depenedency- it runs only once 
import {useEffect} from 'react'

async function getapidata(){
    //api logic
}
useEffect(()=>{
    getapidata()
},[])
3) useEffect with  depenedency values- it will run whenever the depenedency value 
changes
import {useEffect} from 'react'

async function getapidata(){
    //api logic
}
useEffect(()=>{
    getapidata()
},[apidata])














